  "content": {
    "id": "p19-q7-root",
    "type": "question",
    "label": "7",
    "prompt": "Suppose that events $A,B\\subseteq\\Omega$ are independent. Prove that $A'$ and $B$ are also independent.",
    "layout": "list",
    "columns": null,
    "questionDiagrams": [],
    "children": [],
    "answer": {
      "short": "$\\Pr(A'\\cap B)=\\Pr(A')\\Pr(B)$, so $A'$ and $B$ are independent.\n\nSubtract $\\Pr(A\\cap B)$ from $\\Pr(B)$ and use independence.",
      "worked": "Since $A$ and $B$ are independent,\n$$\\begin{align*}\\Pr(A'\\cap B)&=\\Pr(A\\cup B)-\\Pr(A)\\\\\\Pr(A'\\cap B)&=\\Pr(B)-\\Pr(A\\cap B)\\\\\\Pr(A'\\cap B)&=\\Pr(B)-\\Pr(A)\\Pr(B)\\\\\\Pr(A'\\cap B)&=(1-\\Pr(A))\\Pr(B)\\\\\\Pr(A'\\cap B)&=\\Pr(A')\\Pr(B).\\end{align*}$$\nTherefore, $A'$ and $B$ are independent.",
      "solutionDiagrams": []
    },
    "answerSpaceMm": 50
  },
